sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Ambystoma mexicanum Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 184.3 µm (Pass 2) faithfully reproduces Ambystoma mexicanum morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Ambystoma mexicanum specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/ambystoma_mexicanum_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Ambystoma mexicanum; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and diffusion-driven instability | Murray 1981 coat pre-pattern and domain-growth scale argument | Epperlein & Löfberg 1989 larval Ambystoma mexicanum pigment pattern | Frost-Mason & Mason 1996 review of axolotl pigmentation; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters with Du set so the onset wavelength is 184.3 µm | Noise-seeded spectral integration and a shallow source gradient of amplitude 0.12 | Periodic-shell quantization of the continuum wavelength, ratio sweep, and Dv = Du ablation | Quantile segmentation and structure-tensor coherency of the CC BY-SA micrograph; transfer_boundary: 184.3 µm is the slot scale coordinate, not a number measured on the photograph | The source gradient is a reconstruction that keeps the patch from crystallizing; it is not in the constant-coefficient Turing paper | Adult ocellus size is a longer scale of this same Holocene species, not a successor chronospecies; does_not_claim: That stellate melanophore geometry is generated by the PDE | A micrometre scale bar on the Wikimedia micrograph | A second independent assessor]; phenomenon_size: 174 µm (0.0001742 m, log10=-3.759 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 174 µm to 27.9 cm): 174 µm:ambystoma-maculatum-bioelectric-polarity, 324 µm:ambystoma-maculatum-vertex-packing, 6.2 mm:ambystoma-maculatum-turing-wavelength, 1.1 cm:ambystoma-maculatum-clock-wavefront, 3.7 cm:ambystoma-maculatum-morphogen-condensation, 4.8 cm:ambystoma-maculatum-flux-canalization, 5.1 cm:ambystoma-maculatum-elastic-buckling, 6.3 cm:ambystoma-maculatum-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-75056-4>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1007/bf00219740>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1600-0749.1993.tb00611.x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1387/ijdb.8877441> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

